## Summary

**Gate failure root cause (attempt 1).** `state/D9-ricci-flow-surfaces/gate.json` had already been deleted by the dispatcher (`dispatch_loop.py` lines 150–152 remove it right after queuing a repair), so I reproduced the gate exactly (`logs/gate_repair_replay.py`: same `os.walk` pruning, same `cwd` = worktree root, same `ELAN_HOME`/`PATH`, same `lake env lean <abs file>`, 1800 s/file). Exactly four files failed, all from the same cause:

```
release/Poincare/D9/Surfaces/All.lean / AxiomAudit.lean / HomogeneousODE.lean / Statements.lean
error: object file '.../.lake/build/lib/lean/Poincare/D9/Surfaces/Basic.olean'
       of module Poincare.D9.Surfaces.Basic does not exist
```

The compiled D9 artifacts were absent from `release/.lake/build/lib/lean/Poincare/D9/Surfaces/` at gate time. `lake env lean <file>` elaborates but emits no oleans, and the gate visits files alphabetically (`All.lean` before `Basic.lean`), so a missing-olean state fails the gate even though every source is correct. This was a build-artifact defect, not a Lean error.

**Fix (no authored `.lean` changed).** `cd release && lake build Poincare` → exit 0, 8933 jobs, 21.3 s, regenerating `{Basic,All,HomogeneousODE,Statements,AxiomAudit}.{olean,ilean,trace}`. All five authored files remain byte-identical (sha256 matches the original card), with no `sorry`/`axiom`/`unsafe`/`native_decide`/`proof_wanted`; Hamilton and Bernstein–Bando–Shi stay state-only Props and the homogeneous ODE toy theorem remains kernel-checked.

